                <pb facs="0217" n="205" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg205"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/3277: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-24T11:00:00+01:00">May 24, 1940—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 24—8:04 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>844. Your 462, May 23, noon. I delivered the President’s message to the Belgian
                    Ambassador this morning. He informed me that he would transmit it at once to the
                    Belgian Government; but that unfortunately he could not communicate it to King
                    Leopold who was cut off with the French, Belgian, and British Armies now
                    fighting on Belgian soil.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
